<div class="container">
    <div class="grid3">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="eyebrow">Mission</div>
        <h3>Make finance accessible</h3>
        <p>Demystify markets, investing, and financial decision-making for students regardless of prior experience.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="eyebrow">Practice</div>
        <h3>Learn by doing</h3>
        <p>Use market simulators, research companies, build model portfolios, and explain the reasoning behind investment decisions.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="eyebrow">Perspective</div>
        <h3>Connect markets to the world</h3>
        <p>Discuss how interest rates, inflation, technology, geopolitics, and business news influence companies and investors.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section id="about">
      <h2>About the Club</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Founded by Michael, the Investment Club is a student-led community for students interested in finance,
        economics, investing, entrepreneurship, and the forces shaping global markets. The club emphasizes curiosity,
        responsible analysis, discussion, and practical financial literacy rather than short-term speculation.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="michael">
      <div class="bio">
        <div class="portrait" aria-label="Placeholder image for Michael"></div>
        <div class="card bio-copy">
          <div class="eyebrow">Founder & President</div>
          <h2>About Me</h2>
          <p>
            I’m a high school student with a strong interest in finance, economics, investing, and law.
            I founded Michael’s Investment Club to create a place where students can discuss financial markets,
            analyze companies, use stock-market simulators, and develop practical financial knowledge.
          </p>
          <p>
            My interest in finance extends beyond the classroom. I have completed college-level and enrichment
            coursework in financial decision-making and global markets at Stanford University and the University
            of Southern California. I have also gained exposure to private and commercial banking through summer
            job-shadowing experiences, where I learned more about investments, lending, financial planning, and
            how financial institutions serve individuals and businesses.
          </p>
          <p>
            I also created a financial-literacy Instagram platform where I share investing, economic, and
            personal-finance concepts with other students. I believe financial knowledge should be accessible
            to everyone, especially young people who may not have opportunities to study these subjects in school.
          </p>
          <p>
            Through the Investment Club and my broader financial-literacy work, I hope to make complex financial
            topics easier to understand, encourage students to think critically about markets and the economy,
            and help my peers develop financial skills they can use throughout their lives.
          </p>
