    <section id="activities">
      <h2>What We Do</h2>
      <p class="lead">Club meetings combine practical exercises with current-market and economic discussion.</p>
      <div class="topics">
        <div class="topic"><b>Stock Market Simulations</b>Build and monitor model portfolios over time using virtual capital.</div>
        <div class="topic"><b>Company Analysis</b>Review business models, earnings, competitive advantages, valuation, and risk.</div>
        <div class="topic"><b>Economic Discussions</b>Explore interest rates, inflation, employment, trade, technology, and global developments.</div>
        <div class="topic"><b>Investment Thesis Presentations</b>Practice explaining why an investment idea may succeed—and what could go wrong.</div>
        <div class="topic"><b>Portfolio Strategy</b>Discuss diversification, time horizon, risk tolerance, and long-term decision-making.</div>
        <div class="topic"><b>Financial Literacy</b>Cover saving, budgeting, compounding, credit, investing basics, and responsible financial habits.</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="learning">
      <div class="sim">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow">Hands-on learning</div>
          <h2>Think like an investor without risking real money</h2>
          <p class="lead">
            Members can begin with a hypothetical $100,000 portfolio and make investment decisions throughout the semester.
            Performance matters, but the larger goal is to explain the thesis, understand the risk, learn from mistakes,
            and connect portfolio results to real-world market events.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="statbox">
          <div style="opacity:.75">Sample virtual portfolio</div>
          <div class="big">$100,000</div>
          <div style="opacity:.82">Educational simulation • No real capital required</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="callout">
        <div class="eyebrow">Financial Literacy Project</div>
        <h2 style="margin-top:8px">Making finance easier to understand</h2>
        <p class="lead" style="margin-bottom:0">
          Beyond the club, Michael uses social media to share approachable explanations of investing, personal finance,
          economic trends, and market concepts. The goal is to help students build confidence with financial topics
          they may not otherwise encounter in a traditional high-school curriculum.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    
    <section id="insights">
      <div class="eyebrow">New & Noteworthy</div>
      <h2>Market Insights</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        I use this space to share short observations on markets, companies, economic developments,
        and financial-literacy topics. These posts are educational and reflect my own learning process.
      </p>
      <div class="post-grid">
      {% for post in collections.posts | reverse | slice(0, 3) %}
        <a class="post-card" href="{{ post.url }}">
          <div class="post-meta">{{ post.date | readableDate }}</div>
          <h3>{{ post.data.title }}</h3>
          <p>{{ post.data.summary }}</p>
        </a>
      {% endfor %}
      </div>
      <div style="margin-top:18px">
        <a class="social" href="/insights/">View all Market Insights →</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="join">
      <h2>Join Michael's Investment Club</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Michael's Investment Club is designed to be virtual and accessible to students from anywhere.
        No prior investing experience is required—just curiosity, participation, and a willingness to learn.
      </p>
      <div class="card">
        <strong>Virtual Club Information</strong>
        <p><b>Format:</b> Online discussions, market simulations, and virtual learning activities.</p>
        <p><b>Meetings:</b> Held virtually based on member availability and scheduled club sessions.</p>
        <p><b>Who can join:</b> Students interested in investing, economics, financial literacy, and global markets.</p>
        <p><b>How to participate:</b> Follow the club on Instagram and connect through Michael's LinkedIn profile for updates and future virtual sessions.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

